cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use APbase in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "APbase (Rust)"
abstract: >-
  APbase is an intelligent mapping pipeline for irregular field data,
  including yield monitor, soil samples, and sensor grids. It automates the
  map workflow: filtering source data, handling geographic coordinates when
  needed, building the target grid, comparing interpolation methods (IDW,
  ordinary kriging, cokriging), and selecting a ready-to-use map without
  requiring users to choose a mathematical model by hand.
authors:
  - given-names: "Leonardo Felipe"
    family-names: "Maldaner"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2675-767X"
version: "0.1.4"
date-released: "2026-10-17"
license: Apache-2.0
url: "https://apbase.io"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ap-base/apbase-rust"
keywords:
  - geostatistics
  - kriging
  - cokriging
  - interpolation
  - precision agriculture
  - rust
